      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: \n\nYou are likely right about the fact that inconsistent framerate makes it worse.\n\nfor *majority* of the video i am trying to focus both controllers specifically on the letter \"h\", the selection shifts to the direction the headset is accelerating towards.\n\nThe UI sound and \"hover\" effect on the keys is the easiest way to notice the UI's reaction to the head motion.\n\nI already had an image in the post hoping that it would clarify that.\n\nBut yes the video is just a quick demonstration although hard to follow without going frame by frame during a moment the issue occurs.\n\nThe important part is focusing on the text result - knowing i am focusing on a single letter and noticing that occasionally the letter i get is not the one my controllers are focusing on.\n\nThe idea was that \"reproduction steps\" and the description i already had would be enough to understand what i'm trying to do within the video.",
