  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-11T10:53:51.640Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Moving your head/hmd causes UI to jitter. This is particularly problematic for VR Keyboard users, because either your press gets skipped entirely, or it can missclick in the direction your HMD is accelerating to.\n\nWhile spotting the issue itself is easy, it doesn't exactly feel like a big problem when used with \"big UI boxes for browsing content\". But interacting with smaller elements, such as in-game keyboard can become a very difficult task in VR for people with expressive head motions or low/inconsistent performance.\n\nUsing chatbox in VR you have to pretty much keep your head completely static (like a statue) when typing a message to avoid typo's or missing letters.\n\nSteps:\n\n(Unnecessary but optionally you can lower your frame-rate or cause instabilities somehow.)\n\n1. Open your in-game keyboard.\n\n2. Point both of your controllers into a single letter and keep them as static as possible.\n\n3. Swing your head (hmd) around.\n\n4. You should hear a \"UI Selection sound\" as you move your head around (which indicates a different UI element has been hovered over) despite controllers remaining in the same position.\n\nExpected: I should get a letter both of my controllers are pointing at\n\nInstead: I get a letter that my headset is accelerating towards.\n\nVideo: https://youtu.be/MER2TonsPdc\n\nVideo explanation: For the most part I attempt to focus on the \"h\" key as I try to jitter my head, while timing a trigger press with a selection sound. In some cases pressing a trigger results in a letter that my headset was accelerating towards, instead of the letter both of my controllers are pointing at.\n\nEdit: Replaced video link because it went unavailable. Expanded and refined the entire post.",
